From 1a3c87292116662c9158def495eb10267e6c3f90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:38:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] lifecycle guard: refuse shell input computed from
 unresolved substitution output

A shell consumer whose program word, script operand or code argument is the
output of a command substitution ran unscanned: `bash $(echo ./r.sh)`,
`source $(echo ./r.sh)`, `eval "$(cat ./r.sh)"`, `bash -c "$(cat ./r.sh)"`,
`bash <<< "$(cat ./r.sh)"`, and empty splices such as `b$(true)ash ./r.sh` or
`bash ./r$(true).sh`. Real bash runs the script; the guard returned
(False, None).

Why: the scanner removes substitution bodies and walks them separately, so the
consumer word it then reads is a placeholder with no value. Nothing treated a
placeholder at a shell-input position as unknown input.

Change (cron/ only):
- cron/lifecycle_guard_substitution_output.py: at bash/sh/source/./eval/-c/<<<
  consumers, a placeholder in the program, script operand or code argument
  fails closed with "the shell input depends on unresolved command
  substitution output". Empty-in-word splices are also scanned with the
  placeholder removed. The check follows variables, descriptors, functions,
  loops and case arms that carry such a value to a consumer.
- A directly invoked file with a literal Python shebang keeps its whole shell
  walk; only this new check is withheld from its own text, so its verdict
  equals the previous one. Forced `bash f`, `source f`, stdin and scripts it
  references keep the check.
- A placeholder-only basename splice inside a raw quote or printer line whose
  parent has no quote-aware sink is not shell evidence (sed/grep data).
  Single-quoted metacharacters are masked first; heredocs, ANSI-C quotes and
  unbalanced quotes fail closed. The narrowing does not inherit into files or
  nested programs.

Known residual, unchanged from before this commit: a PATH-shadowed `python3`
polyglot with computed shell input is as open as it is today.

Proof: tests/cron/test_lifecycle_guard_substitution_*.py,
test_lifecycle_guard_quoted_provenance.py, test_lifecycle_guard_direct_python*.py
and test_lifecycle_guard_interpreter_identity.py run real bash against a fake
hermes marker and assert the scan verdict; clean python3 variants stay allowed.
